+## drawing the show from stock
+
+A show is designed against the house catalog and fired out of whatever the
+magazine holds. Give any show command `--magazine` and every cue is drawn from
+the book, oldest lot first, and each cue carries the lot number it was drawn
+from onto the cue sheet. Where stock runs out the compiler stands in the
+nearest shell the crew has, preferring the same calibre, and says so; where
+nothing will do it says that instead and the show is not ready. `--pull` sets
+lot numbers aside first, which is what a recall or a wet case means.
+
+```
+portfire check show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig \
+  --magazine magazine.csv --pull vn2405,vn2413
+portfire sheet show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig --magazine magazine.csv
+```
+
 A worked example lives in `examples/autumn`.
 
